# Energy Forecasting

Hourly electricity consumption forecasting using machine learning.

## What I did

* Cleaned and prepared time-series data.
* Created calendar, cyclic, lag and rolling features.
* Trained `HistGradientBoostingRegressor`.
* Used chronological train/test split and `TimeSeriesSplit`.
* Analyzed model errors and feature importance.
* Saved the trained model with Joblib.
* Built a FastAPI prediction API.
* Added Docker and automated tests.
* Added health and Prometheus metrics endpoints.

## Model

`HistGradientBoostingRegressor`

17 features including:

* calendar features;
* cyclic time features;
* lag features;
* rolling averages.

## API

```text
POST /predict
GET  /health
GET  /metrics
```

Swagger:

```text
http://localhost:8015/docs
```

The prediction endpoint requires 169 historical hourly values.

## Run

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Run tests:

```bash
docker compose run --rm energy-api pytest
```

## Tech Stack

Python, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, FastAPI, Pydantic, Joblib, Pytest, Docker.
